# Kconfig — identity component (FW-13).
#
# The two FIRMWARE_IDENTITY_*_MAX_LEN symbols bound the NVS-read
# name + description fields in device_identity_t. Defaults are
# shorter than config.h's CONFIG_IDENTITY_NAME_MAX (32) +
# CONFIG_IDENTITY_DESC_MAX (128) on purpose — FW-13's hello +
# status payloads are short-form (backend parser surface
# minimisation per design smell #2). The softAP /whoami +
# /provision keep the longer config.h caps.

menu "Identity"

    config FIRMWARE_IDENTITY_NAME_MAX_LEN
        int "Identity name max length (bytes; used in hello/status JSON)"
        range 1 128
        default 32
        help
            Maximum byte-length of the `name` field populated from
            NVS `config.name` into device_identity_t. Mirrors the
            cap used by the softAP /whoami endpoint.

    config FIRMWARE_IDENTITY_DESCRIPTION_MAX_LEN
        int "Identity description max length (bytes; used in hello/status JSON)"
        range 1 256
        default 64
        help
            Maximum byte-length of the `description` field populated
            from NVS `config.description` into device_identity_t.
            FW-13's hello + status JSON payloads use 64 (shorter than
            the softAP's 128-byte cap) to minimise parser surface
            area on the backend.

endmenu